  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/0a4b4be4f7de918b847245372077e159f60f3834bb37ef00f4873e63b4cea894.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y={e}^{x}$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{|}_{-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
